# ExItS POS Responsive Data

Authoritative docs:

- `src/Products/PinoyBusinessPOS/Docs/UI/exits-responsive-data-view-standard.md`
- `src/Products/PinoyBusinessPOS/Docs/UI/exits-table-standard.md`

Also: `EXITS_UI_STANDARD.md`, visual reference `/ui-standards`

## Default for collections

When presenting a collection/list of structured records, use **`ExitsResponsiveDataView`** — do not invent a page-specific responsive table.

| Viewport | Presentation |
|----------|----------------|
| Desktop | **TABLE** via `ExitsTable` |
| Tablet | Keep TABLE only if content fits comfortably; otherwise LIST / record-card |
| Mobile | **LIST** / `ExitsDataRecordCard` by default |

Do **not** force horizontal table scrolling as the default mobile solution.  
Horizontal scroll is allowed only for an explicit dense-grid exception.

## Column priority

Use column priority metadata:

- Primary
- Secondary
- Detail
- HiddenOnCompact

Mobile/list records prioritize: main identity → important secondary identity → key values → status → **one** primary quick action → remaining under **More**.  
Do not show every desktop column equally on mobile.

## Actions by mode

**TABLE mode**

- Existing row-action pattern
- Multi-select allowed when needed
- Sorting / filtering / pagination available

**LIST mode**

- At most one primary quick action where practical
- Additional actions under More
- Multi-select **OFF** by default; opt-in only when mobile bulk ops genuinely matter

## Shared dataset logic

Search, filter, and pagination must operate on the **same dataset** regardless of TABLE vs LIST presentation.  
Do **not** create separate desktop/mobile business logic.

## Auto-infer

User asks for a “list” / “table” / collection without specifying presentation → choose `ExitsResponsiveDataView` (desktop table, responsive cards on smaller screens).

## Exceptions

Preserve domain correctness when an existing workflow genuinely needs another pattern; document why. Prefer reuse + this standard when uncertain.
